cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "SeabedNet: model-completed bathymetry and shoal hazard for Canadian waters"
message: "If you use this software, the benchmark or the results, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Girard
    given-names: Emilio
    city: Montréal
    country: CA
repository-code: "https://github.com/girardemilio3-svg/seabednet"
url: "https://girardemilio3-svg.github.io/churchill-corridor-atlas/"
abstract: >-
  A masked-completion neural network that fills the gaps between published
  soundings in Canadian waters with depth, calibrated uncertainty and
  provenance, together with a shoal-hazard model, a reusable temporal
  benchmark, and prospective forecasts sealed before their outcomes.
keywords: [bathymetry, hydrography, Arctic, machine learning, uncertainty, Canada]
